wh:site_1024 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "مدن الفن الباروكيّ المتأخر في وادي نوتو"@ar,
        "Late Baroque Towns of the Val di Noto (South-Eastern Sicily)"@en,
        "Ciudades del barroco tardío del Valle de Noto (sudeste de Sicilia)"@es,
        "Villes du baroque tardif de la vallée de Noto (sud-est de la Sicile)"@fr,
        "Города позднего барокко в районе Валь-ди-Ното, юго-восток острова Сицилия"@ru,
        "晚期的巴洛克城镇瓦拉迪那托（西西里东南部）"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 112.79 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "The eight towns in south-eastern Sicily: Caltagirone, Militello Val di Catania, Catania, Modica, Noto, Palazzolo, Ragusa and Scicli, were all rebuilt after 1693 on or beside towns existing at the time of the earthquake which took place in that year. They represent a considerable collective undertaking, successfully carried out at a high level of architectural and artistic achievement. Keeping within the late Baroque style of the day, they also depict distinctive innovations in town planning and urban building."@en ;
    wh:hasCategory wh:category_Cultural ;
    wh:hasComponent wh:component_1024-001,
        wh:component_1024-002,
        wh:component_1024-003,
        wh:component_1024-004,
