wh:site_136 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "حديقة غارامبا الوطنية"@ar,
        "Garamba National Park"@en,
        "Parque Nacional de Garamba"@es,
        "Parc national de la Garamba"@fr,
        "Национальный парк Гарамба"@ru,
        "阿米勒山区城堡群"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 512736.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_AFR ;
    wh:description "The property, located in the north-eastern Democratic Republic of the Congo, forms part of one of the last extensive and continuous forest–savanna mosaic landscapes in Central Africa. Representing a major ecological transition zone between the Guineo-Congolian forest biome and the Sudanian savanna, it encompasses a diverse range of habitats, including grasslands, wooded savannas, semi-deciduous forests, rivers, gallery forests, marshes, and papyrus wetlands. Ecological processes such as fire, herbivory, and seasonal flooding continue to shape the landscape and maintain its forest–savanna dynamics. The park supports a rich assemblage of wildlife, including significant populations of African Forest Elephants, Kordofan Giraffes, Common Hippopotamuses, African buffaloes, lions, pangolins, and numerous primate species. It is home to more than 150 mammal species, 459 bird species, 83 reptile species, and 43 amphibian species, including threatened and regional endemic species."@en ;
