wh:site_1376 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "بريدجتاون التاريخية وحاميتها"@ar,
        "Historic Bridgetown and its Garrison"@en,
        "El Centro histórico de Bridgetown y su guarnición militar"@es,
        "Centre historique de Bridgetown et sa garnison"@fr,
        "Исторический Бриджтаун с его военными укреплениями"@ru,
        "布里奇顿及其军事要塞"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 187.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_LAC ;
    wh:description "Historic Bridgetown and its Garrison, an outstanding example of British colonial architecture consisting of a well-preserved old town built in the 17th, 18th and 19th centuries, which testifies to the spread of Great Britain's Atlantic colonial empire. The property also includes a nearby military garrison which consists of numerous historic buildings. With its serpentine urban lay-out the property testifies to a different approach to colonial town-planning compared to the Spanish and Dutch colonial cities of the region which were built along a grid plan."@en ;
