wh:site_1469 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "موقع الصيد بالمطاردة في جوتلاند الشمالية"@ar,
        "The par force hunting landscape in North Zealand"@en,
        "Paisaje cinegético de montería de Selandia Septentrional"@es,
        "Paysage de chasse à courre de Zélande du Nord"@fr,
        "Охотничьи угодья Северной Зеландии"@ru,
        "北西兰岛狩猎园林"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 4543.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "Located about 30 km northeast of Copenhagen, this cultural landscape encompasses the two hunting forests of Store Dyrehave and Gribskov, as well as the hunting park of Jægersborg Hegn/Jægersborg Dyrehave. This is a designed landscape where Danish kings and their court practiced par force hunting, or hunting with hounds, which reached its peak between the 17th and the late 18th centuries, when the absloute monarchs transformed it into a landscape of power. With hunting lanes laid out in a star system, combined with an orthogonal grid pattern, numbered stone posts, fences and a hunting lodge, the site demonstrates the application of Baroque landscaping principles to forested areas."@en ;
