wh:site_1586 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "مواقع ذكرى الإبادة الجماعية: نياماتا ومورامبي وجيسوزي وبيسسيرو"@ar,
        "Memorial sites of the Genocide: Nyamata, Murambi, Gisozi and Bisesero"@en,
        "Sitios conmemorativos del Genocidio: Nyamata, Murambi, Gisozi y Bisesero"@es,
        "Sites mémoriaux du génocide : Nyamata, Murambi, Gisozi et Bisesero"@fr,
        "Мемориальные комплексы геноцида: Ньямата, Мурамби, Гисози и Бисеро"@ru,
        "种族大屠杀纪念地：恩亚玛塔、穆拉姆比、吉索兹和比瑟瑟罗"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 24.65 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_AFR ;
    wh:description "Between April and July 1994, an estimated one million people were killed across Rwanda by armed militias called Interahamwe that targeted Tutsi, but also executed moderate Hutu and Twa people. The victims of the genocide are commemorated in this serial property composed of four memorial sites. Two of the component parts were scenes of massacres: a Catholic church built in the hill of Nyamata in 1980, and a technical school built in the hill of Murambi in 1990. The hill of Gisozi in Kigali City hosts the Kigali Genocide Memorial built in 1999, where more than 250,000 victims have been buried, while the hill of Bisesero in the Western Province hosts a memorial built in 1998, to remember the fight of those who resisted their perpetrators for over two months before being exterminated."@en ;
