wh:site_1765 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "مواقع صناعة الخزف التقليدية في جينغدتشن"@ar,
        "Jingdezhen Handicraft Porcelain Industry Sites"@en,
        "Sitios de producción de porcelana artesanal de Jingdezhen"@es,
        "Sites de l’industrie de la porcelaine artisanale de Jingdezhen"@fr,
        "Объекты ремесленного фарфорового производства Цзиндэчжэня"@ru,
        "景德镇手工瓷业遗存"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 1979.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_APA ;
    wh:description "The serial property portrays the evolution of the production of handicraft porcelain from the 10th to 19th centuries that had profound industrial, artistic and trading influences in China and beyond globally. The five component parts reflect the processes of the production of porcelain, including the extraction and transportation of raw materials, innovations in kiln design and the spatial and social organisation of production on an immense scale. The town area featured the Imperial Kiln alongside civilian kilns, guilds and merchant associations. Jingdezhen was a centre of technological innovation in porcelain production, including the “binary formula” of mixing kaolin and porcelain stone. Porcelain of the highest quality was produced at Jingdezhen, and its blue-and-white porcelain and designs became a prized global commodity and a symbol of Chinese culture and artistry."@en ;
    wh:hasCategory wh:category_Cultural ;
    wh:hasComponent wh:component_1765-001,
        wh:component_1765-002,
        wh:component_1765-003,
