wh:site_1766 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "Tashkent Modernist Architecture. Modernity and Tradition in Central Asia"@en,
        "Arquitectura modernista de Tashkent. Modernidad y tradición en Asia Central"@es,
        "Architecture moderniste de Tachkent. Modernité et tradition en Asie centrale"@fr,
        "Модернистская архитектура Ташкента. Современность и традиция в Центральной Азии"@ru,
        "塔什干现代主义建筑：中亚的现代性和传统"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 62.588 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_APA ;
    wh:description "The property embodies a representative ensemble of ten modernist buildings and urban complexes constructed between the 1960s and early 1990s, a formative period in the reconstruction and transformation of Tashkent following the 1966 earthquake. The series includes museums, exhibition halls, residential ensembles, cultural institutions, and scientific or infrastructural facilities, reflecting the broad functional spectrum of late‑Soviet architectural production. Nine out of ten component parts are situated along the newly planned urban axes of the reconstructed city centre, as defined in successive masterplans that reshaped Tashkent into a modern socialist metropolis. Together, they articulate the city’s principal public spaces and demonstrate the integration of modernist planning principles with local climatic, seismic, and cultural conditions. Collectively, the serial property illustrates a distinct phase of architectural modernism characterised by industrialised construction, seismic‑resilient engineering, and the adaptation of standardised systems to regional materials, traditions, and environmental constraints."@en ;
    wh:hasCategory wh:category_Cultural ;
    wh:hasComponent wh:component_1766-001,
