    wh:areaHectares 11800.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "The nature reserve, which is part of the Regional Natural Park of Corsica, occupies the Scandola peninsula, an impressive, porphyritic rock mass. The vegetation is an outstanding example of scrubland. Seagulls, cormorants and sea eagles can be found there. The clear waters, with their islets and inaccessible caves, host a rich marine life."@en ;
