wh:site_357 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "منتزه غوريم الوطني ومواقع كابادوس  الصخرية"@ar,
        "Göreme National Park and the Rock Sites of Cappadocia"@en,
        "Parque Nacional de Göreme y sitios rupestres de Capadocia"@es,
        "Parc national de Göreme et sites rupestres de Cappadoce"@fr,
        "Национальный парк Гёреме и пещерные постройки Каппадокии"@ru,
        "希拉波利斯和帕姆卡莱"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 9883.81 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "In a spectacular landscape, entirely sculpted by erosion, the Göreme valley and its surroundings contain rock-hewn sanctuaries that provide unique evidence of Byzantine art in the post-Iconoclastic period. Dwellings, troglodyte villages and underground towns – the remains of a traditional human habitat dating back to the 4th century – can also be seen there."@en ;
