wh:site_415 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "الوسط التاريخي في اواكساكا والمنطقة الأثرية في مونتي ألبان"@ar,
        "Historic Centre of Oaxaca and Archaeological Site of Monte Albán"@en,
        "Centro histórico de Oaxaca y zona arqueológica de Monte Albán"@es,
        "Centre historique de Oaxaca et zone archéologique de Monte Alban"@fr,
        "Историческая часть города Оахака и центр древней индейской культуры Монте-Альбан"@ru,
        "瓦哈卡历史中心与阿尔班山考古遗址"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 4375.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_LAC ;
    wh:description "Inhabited over a period of 1,500 years by a succession of peoples – Olmecs, Zapotecs and Mixtecs – the terraces, dams, canals, pyramids and artificial mounds of Monte Albán were literally carved out of the mountain and are the symbols of a sacred topography. The nearby city of Oaxaca, which is built on a grid pattern, is a good example of Spanish colonial town planning. The solidity and volume of the city's buildings show that they were adapted to the earthquake-prone region in which these architectural gems were constructed."@en ;
    wh:hasCategory wh:category_Cultural ;
