wh:site_481 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "معبد فات فو والمنشآت القديمة الملحقة بالمنظر الثقافي في مقاطعة تشامباساك"@ar,
        "Vat Phou and Associated Ancient Settlements within the Champasak Cultural Landscape"@en,
        "Vat Phu y antiguos poblamientos anejos del paisaje cultural de Champasak"@es,
        "Vat Phou et les anciens établissements associés du paysage culturel de Champassak"@fr,
        "Культурный ландшафт Тямпасак с храмовым комплексом Ват-Фу и окружающими древними поселениями"@ru,
        "占巴塞文化景观内的瓦普庙和相关古民居"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 39000.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_APA ;
    wh:description "The Champasak cultural landscape, including the Vat Phou Temple complex, is a remarkably well-preserved planned landscape more than 1,000 years old. It was shaped to express the Hindu vision of the relationship between nature and humanity, using an axis from mountain top to river bank to lay out a geometric pattern of temples, shrines and waterworks extending over some 10 km. Two planned cities on the banks of the Mekong River are also part of the site, as well as Phou Kao mountain. The whole represents a development ranging from the 5th to 15th centuries, mainly associated with the Khmer Empire."@en ;
