wh:site_529 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "الإرساليات اليسوعية في محافظة الـ تشيكيتوس"@ar,
        "Jesuit Missions of the Chiquitos"@en,
        "Misiones jesuí­ticas de Chiquitos"@es,
        "Missions jésuites de Chiquitos"@fr,
        "Иезуитские миссии на землях индейцев чикитос"@ru,
        "奇基托斯耶稣传教区"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 0.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_LAC ;
    wh:description "Between 1696 and 1760, six ensembles of reducciones (settlements of Christianized Indians) inspired by the ‘ideal cities’ of the 16th-century philosophers were founded by the Jesuits in a style that married Catholic architecture with local traditions. The six that remain – San Francisco Javier, Concepción, Santa Ana, San Miguel, San Rafael and San José – make up a living heritage on the former territory of the Chiquitos."@en ;
