wh:site_549 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "القصر الملكي للقرن الثامن عشر في كازيرتا  مع الحديقة وقناة فانفيتيلّي  ومجموعة سان لوتشيو"@ar,
        "18th-Century Royal Palace at Caserta with the Park, the Aqueduct of Vanvitelli, and the San Leucio Complex"@en,
        "Palacio Real del siglo XVIII de Caserta con el parque, el acueducto de Vanvitelli y el conjunto de San Leucio"@es,
        "Palais royal du XVIIIe siècle de Caserte avec le parc, l’aqueduc de Vanvitelli et l’ensemble de San Leucio"@fr,
        "Королевский дворец XVIII в. с парком в Казерте, акведук Ванвителли и фабричный поселок Сан-Леучо"@ru,
        "卡塞塔的18世纪花园皇宫、凡韦特里水渠和圣莱乌西建筑群"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 87.37 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "The monumental complex at Caserta, created by the Bourbon king Charles III in the mid-18th century to rival Versailles and the Royal Palace in Madrid, is exceptional for the way in which it brings together a magnificent palace with its park and gardens, as well as natural woodland, hunting lodges and a silk factory. It is an eloquent expression of the Enlightenment in material form, integrated into, rather than imposed on, its natural setting."@en ;
    wh:hasCategory wh:category_Cultural ;
    wh:hasComponent wh:component_549rev ;
    wh:hasCriterion wh:criterion_i,
        wh:criterion_ii,
