wh:site_665 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "دير سانتا ماريا دي غوادالوبي الملكي"@ar,
        "Royal Monastery of Santa María de Guadalupe"@en,
        "Real Monasterio de Santa María de Guadalupe"@es,
        "Monastère royal de Santa María de Guadalupe"@fr,
        "Королевский монастырь Санта-Мария-де-Гуадалупе"@ru,
        "瓜达卢佩的圣玛利皇家修道院"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 1.1 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "The monastery is an outstanding repository of four centuries of Spanish religious architecture. It symbolizes two significant events in world history that occurred in 1492: the Reconquest of the Iberian peninsula by the Catholic Kings and Christopher Columbus' arrival in the Americas. Its famous statue of the Virgin became a powerful symbol of the Christianization of much of the New World."@en ;
