wh:site_666 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "لومبيني، مكان ولادة بوذا"@ar,
        "Lumbini, the Birthplace of the Lord Buddha"@en,
        "Lumbini, lugar de nacimiento de Buda"@es,
        "Lumbini, lieu de naissance du Bouddha"@fr,
        "Лумбини, место рождения Будды"@ru,
        "佛祖诞生地兰毗尼"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 1.95 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_APA ;
    wh:description "Siddhartha Gautama, the Lord Buddha, was born in 623 B.C. in the famous gardens of Lumbini, which soon became a place of pilgrimage. Among the pilgrims was the Indian emperor Ashoka, who erected one of his commemorative pillars there. The site is now being developed as a Buddhist pilgrimage centre, where the archaeological remains associated with the birth of the Lord Buddha form a central feature."@en ;
