wh:site_725 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "كهوف ذات طوبوغرافية كارست في قرية أغتليك  المجرية وسلوفاكيا"@ar,
        "Caves of Aggtelek Karst and Slovak Karst"@en,
        "Grutas del karst de Aggtelek y del karst de Eslovaquia"@es,
        "Grottes du karst d'Aggtelek et du karst de Slovaquie"@fr,
        "Пещерный район Аггтелек – Словацкий карст"@ru,
        "阿格泰列克洞穴和斯洛伐克喀斯特地貌"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 56650.57 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "The variety of formations and the fact that they are concentrated in a restricted area means that the 712 caves currently identified make up a typical temperate-zone karstic system. Because they display an extremely rare combination of tropical and glacial climatic effects, they make it possible to study geological history over tens of millions of years."@en ;
