wh:site_732 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "كوتنا هورا: وسط المدينة التاريخي وكنيسة سانتا باربرا وكاتدرائية السيدة في سدلك"@ar,
        "Kutná Hora: Historical Town Centre with the Church of St Barbara and the Cathedral of Our Lady at Sedlec"@en,
        "Kutná Hora: centro histórico de la ciudad,iglesia de Santa Bárbara y catedral de Nuestra Señora de Sedlec"@es,
        "Kutná Hora : le centre historique de la ville avec l'église Sainte-Barbe et la cathédrale Notre-Dame de Sedlec"@fr,
        "Кутна-Гора: исторический центр города с церковью Св. Варвары и кафедральным собором Богородицы в Седлеце"@ru,
        "库特纳霍拉历史名城中心的圣巴拉巴教堂及塞德莱茨的圣母玛利亚大教堂"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 62.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "Kutná Hora developed as a result of the exploitation of the silver mines. In the 14th century it became a royal city endowed with monuments that symbolized its prosperity. The Church of St Barbara, a jewel of the late Gothic period, and the Cathedral of Our Lady at Sedlec, which was restored in line with the Baroque taste of the early 18th century, were to influence the architecture of central Europe. These masterpieces today form part of a well-preserved medieval urban fabric with some particularly fine private dwellings."@en ;
    wh:hasCategory wh:category_Cultural ;
    wh:hasComponent wh:component_732-001,
        wh:component_732-002 ;
    wh:hasCriterion wh:criterion_ii,
        wh:criterion_iv ;
    wh:hasImage wh:image_006955ac5da35623,
        wh:image_08f9383c1953f582,
        wh:image_1aa7ed005fd5f104,
        wh:image_248ee3a1ae4d566e,
        wh:image_35b02856c16be6eb,
        wh:image_377ef3522ea5f605,
        wh:image_37dce037cb0ad9fa,
