wh:site_792 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "منطقة النصب التاريخية في كويريتارو"@ar,
        "Historic Monuments Zone of Querétaro"@en,
        "Zona de monumentos históricos de Querétaro"@es,
        "Zone de monuments historiques de Querétaro"@fr,
        "Зона исторических памятников в городе Керетаро"@ru,
        "克雷塔罗历史遗迹区"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 258.3 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_LAC ;
    wh:description "The old colonial town of Querétaro is unusual in having retained the geometric street plan of the Spanish conquerors side by side with the twisting alleys of the Indian quarters. The Otomi, the Tarasco, the Chichimeca and the Spanish lived together peacefully in the town, which is notable for the many ornate civil and religious Baroque monuments from its golden age in the 17th and 18th centuries."@en ;
