wh:site_847 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "قصر مالبورك المبني وفقًا للنمط التوتوني"@ar,
        "Castle of the Teutonic Order in Malbork"@en,
        "Castillo de la Orden Teutónica en Malbork"@es,
        "Château de l’ordre Teutonique de Malbork"@fr,
        "Замок Тевтонского Ордена в городе Мальборк"@ru,
        "马尔堡的条顿骑士团城堡"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 18.038 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "This 13th-century fortified monastery belonging to the Teutonic Order was substantially enlarged and embellished after 1309, when the seat of the Grand Master moved here from Venice. A particularly fine example of a medieval brick castle, it later fell into decay, but was meticulously restored in the 19th and early 20th centuries. Many of the conservation techniques now accepted as standard were evolved here. Following severe damage in the Second World War it was once again restored, using the detailed documentation prepared by earlier conservators."@en ;
