wh:site_850 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "وادي قاديشا أو الوادي المقدس وحرش أرز الرب"@ar,
        "Ouadi Qadisha (the Holy Valley) and the Forest of the Cedars of God (Horsh Arz el-Rab)"@en,
        "Valle Santo (Uadi Qadisha) y Bosque de los cedros de Dios (Horsh Arz Al Rab)"@es,
        "Ouadi Qadisha ou Vallée sainte et forêt des cèdres de Dieu (Horsh Arz el-Rab)"@fr,
        "Священная Долина (Уади-Кадиша) и Божественная Кедровая Роща (Хорш-Арз-эль-Раб)"@ru,
        "夸底•夸底沙(圣谷)和神杉林"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 1720.2 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_ARB ;
    wh:description "The Qadisha valley is one of the most important early Christian monastic settlements in the world. Its monasteries, many of which are of a great age, stand in dramatic positions in a rugged landscape. Nearby are the remains of the great forest of cedars of Lebanon, highly prized in antiquity for the construction of great religious buildings."@en ;
    wh:hasCategory wh:category_Cultural ;
