wh:site_91 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "وسط روما التاريخي، أملاك الكرسي الرسولي الواقع في هذه المدينة والتي تتمتع بحقوق الحصانة السياسية وسان بول فيوري لي مورا"@ar,
        "Historic Centre of Rome, the Properties of the Holy See in that City Enjoying Extraterritorial Rights and San Paolo Fuori le Mura"@en,
        "Centro Histórico de Roma, los bienes de la Santa Sede beneficiarios del derecho de extraterritorialidad situados en la ciudad y San Pablo Extramuros"@es,
        "Centre historique de Rome, les biens du Saint-Siège situés dans cette ville bénéficiant des droits d'extra-territorialité et Saint-Paul-hors-les-Murs"@fr,
        "Исторический центр Рима и владения Ватикана, пользующиеся правами экстерриториальности, включая церковь Сан-Паоло-Фуори-ле-Мура"@ru,
        "罗马历史中心，享受治外法权的罗马教廷建筑和缪拉圣保罗弗利"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 1469.7 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "Founded, according to legend, by Romulus and Remus in 753 BC, Rome was first the centre of the Roman Republic, then of the Roman Empire, and it became the capital of the Christian world in the 4th century. The World Heritage site, extended in 1990 to the walls of Urban VIII, includes some of the major monuments of antiquity such as the Forums, the Mausoleum of Augustus, the Mausoleum of Hadrian, the Pantheon, Trajan’s Column and the Column of Marcus Aurelius, as well as the religious and public buildings of papal Rome."@en ;
