wh:site_942 a wh:WorldHeritageSite ;
    rdfs:label "موقع كورا التاريخي ودير مار يوحنا اللاهوتي ومغارة نهاية العالم على جزيرة باتموس"@ar,
        "The Historic Centre (Chorá) with the Monastery of Saint-John the Theologian and the Cave of the Apocalypse on the Island of Pátmos"@en,
        "Centro histórico (Chorá) con el monasterio de San Juan “el Teólogo” y la gruta del Apocalipsis en la isla de Patmos"@es,
        "Centre historique (Chorá) avec le monastère de Saint Jean « le théologien » et la grotte de l'Apocalypse sur l'île de Patmos"@fr,
        "Исторический центр (Хора) с монастырем Иоанна Богослова и пещерой Апокалипсиса на острове Патмос"@ru,
        "帕特莫斯岛的天启洞穴和圣约翰修道院"@zh ;
    wh:areaHectares 0.0 ;
    wh:belongsToRegion wh:region_EUR ;
    wh:description "The small island of Pátmos in the Dodecanese is reputed to be where St John the Theologian wrote both his Gospel and the Apocalypse. A monastery dedicated to the ‘beloved disciple’ was founded there in the late 10th century and it has been a place of pilgrimage and Greek Orthodox learning ever since. The fine monastic complex dominates the island. The old settlement of Chorá, associated with it, contains many religious and secular buildings."@en ;
